# Automated data PRs append one record per run to shared time-series
# files under data/, so two PRs open at the same time always conflict at
# end-of-file as soon as one of them merges. The correct resolution is
# always the union of both sides' appended lines, which is what git's
# built-in "union" merge driver produces. Record order within a file does
# not matter: consumers (e.g. tools/summarize_layers.py) sort by the
# datestamp embedded in each record.
#
# Note that GitHub's PR conflict detection ignores merge drivers, so
# conflicted data PRs are re-merged server-side by the heal-data-prs
# workflow (tools/heal-data-prs.sh), which relies on these attributes.
data/**/*.jsonl merge=union
data/**/*.csv merge=union
data/**/*.csv.checkpoint merge=union
